    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe following ftplugins use `term_start` that is not available in nvim:\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/544d8cd7e6289ca98e9104b55cdb963eeda51755/runtime/ftplugin/ps1.vim#L56\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/544d8cd7e6289ca98e9104b55cdb963eeda51755/runtime/ftplugin/sh.vim#L58\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/544d8cd7e6289ca98e9104b55cdb963eeda51755/runtime/ftplugin/zsh.vim#L28\n\nConsequently a keywordprg does not work: `E117: Unknown function :term_start`.\n\n(I&rsquo;m not sure whether this should go to vim or nvim.)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```bash\nnvim --clean - << EOF\n#!/bin/bash\npwd\nEOF\n```\n\nPress <kbd>K</kbd> on the pwd.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n<kbd>K</kbd> works.\n\n`term_start` is replaced with `jobstart` (or `lua vim.system`).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n2f047b56683e8823ab1064a512e7faca0ba5e0bb\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.1178\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
